core: Super Fly II 700G Core with Dualzone EGD and Squeezebox
core wood: Stronger and lighter woods targeted in specific areas for more pop and strength while reducing weight
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain aligned along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to the rest of the core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker, more powerful sections combined with thinner, more flexible sections profiled throughout core, enhances energy transfer, snappier and more stable)
edges: Frostbite Edges (edges extend out slightly underneath bindings for enhanced edge hold on hardpack and ice)
base: Sintered WFO (extra absorbent, high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax, ultra durable)
board break-in technology: Infinite Ride (overbuilt in factory then broken down by machinery so the board rides the same from day one to day 100, season after season)
tip/tail technology: Pro-Tip (tip and tail taper out at the points, reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin that reduces carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
alternative version: Also comes in Burton's Flying-V bend for a more forgiving and versatile ride
legacy: Cult classic backed by 30 years of good times, podium finishes, and all mountain performance
